speechtext:
I need not see the Bill;
I have the resolution. I say that the Government, by the appointments which have been made since the recent elections, such as the appointment of the postmaster of Ottawa, whjch has aroused the anger not only of Liberals but of Conservatives, and
46*
similar appointments made throughout the country, has shown that patronage has not been abolished. Yet when we ask for an explanation from the Acting Minister of Finance, he does not give us any explanation, he simply says:	The hour is late;
let us pass the resolution, and I shall introduce my Bill. We on this side of the House are willing to support all measures which the Government prove to us are good.
